  enforceMaxStress: 0
  maxAllowedStress: 100
  isTimeAttack: 0
  timeAttackDuration: 60
  winCondition: 0
  requiredIntactTime: 5
  goldReward: 500
  expReward: 100
  offerDialogue:
    name: Clark
    sentences:
    - Alright, let's put those materials and that new bridge type to use.
    - We need a crossing that connects the freight yard directly to the warehouse
      district.
    - We'll test it with <b><#E09500>four cargo trucks, two travelling in each direction</color></b>.
      The bridge must support them safely throughout the crossing.
    - You have the <b><#E09500>steel components</color></b> available. Make sure
      the roadway, hangers, cables, towers, and anchorages form a structure that
      can safely carry the load.
    - Take a good look at the site before you decide how to build it. If you're ready,
      I'll hand over the contract.
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Clark
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Clark
    sentences:
    - Don't rush into changing the whole design if the test doesn't go well. <b><#E09500>Check
      how the components connect and where the structure needs more support</color></b>.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Clark
    sentences:
    - That should make things easier for the freight crews. They can move cargo between
      the yard and the warehouses without going all the way around the factory blocks.
    - You've also seen how a <b><#E09500>Suspension Bridge</color></b> uses cables,
      hangers, towers, and anchorages to support its roadway.
    - That was a longer span than the crossings you handled in Town River, but you
      managed it well, {PlayerName}.
    - I have another site farther into the factory district. The challenge there
      is a little different, so we'll need to approach it another way.
